<title>JAPAN: TABLE-Japan July trade surplus up 69.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Japan July trade surplus up 69.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's contentious trade surplus rose for the fourth successive month in July, surging 69.7 percent from a year earlier to 849.08 billion yen, the Finance Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The customs-cleared trade surplus with the United States, often a source of friction, jumped 35.7 percent in July from a year earlier to 420.55 billion yen. The figures were not adjusted for seasonal factors.  </p>
